# Activating a stored graph
#
# A fact stores a quoted graph as its value. An N3 rule binds that value
# and uses it directly as the conclusion, making the graph's statement
# available as a derived fact.

@base <https://eyereasoner.github.io/eye/reasoning/iq/iq-extra.n3> .

@prefix : <http://example.org/test#> .

# The fact: the object of :a :b is a quoted graph, a formula in braces.
:a :b {
    :c :d :e
} .

# The rule: its conclusion is the variable ?y itself, so whatever graph ?y
# is bound to becomes the set of derived statements.
{
    ?x :b ?y
} => ?y .
